      "writtenOn": "2024-06-21T18:03:31Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "The whole point of this method/utiliy is to restore the permission after being done executing.\n\nThis change is completely removing the feature.\n\nUnfortunately in BluetoothServiceBinderTest we are not using this utility at all. You are comparing a unit test that doesn\u0027t intent to check permission at all vs cts tests.\n\nFor example `SystemBluetoothTest.java` is taking CONNECT and PRIVILEGED in [setup](https://source.corp.google.com/h/googleplex-android/platform/superproject/main/+/main:cts/tests/tests/bluetooth/src/android/bluetooth/cts/SystemBluetoothTest.java;l\u003d85;drc\u003d985e9f23a965bdd0e59900b3f33b0fbe9319b884), and in test it [start](https://source.corp.google.com/h/googleplex-android/platform/superproject/main/+/main:cts/tests/tests/bluetooth/src/android/bluetooth/cts/SystemBluetoothTest.java;l\u003d157;drc\u003d985e9f23a965bdd0e59900b3f33b0fbe9319b884) a discovery with the SCAN permission only.\n\nAfter the call, it should have CONNECT and PRIVILEGED.\n\n----\n\nInstead, please, check for a size \u003d\u003d 0 before dropping the identity\n\n```suggestion\n        if (UiAutomation.ALL_PERMISSIONS.equals(permissions)) {\n            uiAutomation.adoptShellPermissionIdentity()\n        } else if (permissions.size() \u003d\u003d 0) {\n            uiAutomation.dropShellPermissionIdentity()\n        } else {\n            uiAutomation.adoptShellPermissionIdentity(*permissions.map { it }.toTypedArray())\n        }\n```",
